<title>ITALY: Italy's Bari sees March CPI at -0.2 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Bari sees March CPI at -0.2 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>BARI, Italy 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Bari said its March consumer price index stood at -0.2 percent month on month and 1.8 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In February, Bari inflation rate was 0.0 percent and 2.3 percent respectively. The general index and the housing and utility charges sector have been revised to take account of a court ruling that reversed electricity tariff reductions.</p>
<p>Bari is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data on Thursday and Friday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 5.99 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to February 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		    -0.2     (0.0R)  1.8    (2.3R)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.1    (-0.3)   0.2    (0.6)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0     (0.0)   1.9    (2.1)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.2     (0.7R)  6.1    (5.9R)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.1    (-0.2)   1.5    (1.9)</p>
<p>    Health services		  -0.3     (0.2)   3.5    (4.6)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.3     (0.3)   6.2    (6.4)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -1.1     (0.1)  -0.6    (1.1)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0     (0.0)   3.9    (7.8)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	 -0.8     (0.0)   0.6    (1.1)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0     (0.2)   0.7    (0.7)</p>
<p>R - revised</p>
<p>-- Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
